# What the sdist carries beyond setuptools' defaults (the package, README, pyproject
# and the license files). The wheel is unaffected: its contents come from
# [tool.setuptools.packages.find] in pyproject.toml.
#
# The sdist is meant to be testable, because downstream packagers (conda-forge among
# them) run the suite from it. It therefore carries the whole library test suite and
# the documents README links to.
graft tests
graft docs
include CHANGELOG.md ACKNOWLEDGMENTS.md

# tests/tooling checks the repository's own tooling (tools/, benchmarks/, .github/),
# none of which the sdist ships, so those tests could only fail there.
prune tests/tooling

# A local build from a working tree must not pack the bytecode caches.
global-exclude *.py[cod]
